--- A. UNIQUE INVARIANT MEASURE? ---
  lattice diag(1.0,1.0)Z^2: h_(a^2) returns (y 1.0000 -> 1.0000); period a^2 = 1.000; orbit average of 1[|v1|^2<0.5] = 0.000  (Haar 0.477)
  lattice diag(0.5,2.0)Z^2: h_(a^2) returns (y 4.0000 -> 4.0000); period a^2 = 0.250; orbit average of 1[|v1|^2<0.5] = 1.000  (Haar 0.477)
  lattice diag(0.2,5.0)Z^2: h_(a^2) returns (y 25.0000 -> 25.0000); period a^2 = 0.040; orbit average of 1[|v1|^2<0.5] = 1.000  (Haar 0.477)
  => a one-parameter family of periodic orbits, each carrying its own invariant probability measure;
     their averages (0, 1, ...) differ from Haar. A FAILS on non-compact X2 (Dani: Haar + periodic-orbit measures).

